description:
At Alexa Shopping Science team (from Mar 2021), my current responsibilities are:
1) Leading research on bias mitigation technologies in NLP to enhance fairness while preserving user privacy;
2) Building and deploying ML solutions in creating unified user experiences for Alexa Shopping across different devices;
3) Working in cross-functional teams, overseeing prototype to production, and communicating results with stakeholders;
4) Supervising research internships and coaching and mentoring junior team members.

At Alexa Text-to-Speech Research team (Nov 2019 - Feb 2021), I had:
1) Proposed and delivered a deep generative model for 'universal' speech synthesis, which can be used regardless of speaker identity or language and can therefore massively save cost in TTS production and speed up launch of new TTS voices;
2) Collaborated with engineers to scale up Alexa TTS production and launch new voices in multiple regions and countries.

At Take BLip, I had the opportunity to not only enhance my hard skills but also develop my soft skills. As part of my role, I served as a technical reference for the team, clients, and partners. I provided guidance and expertise in solution architecture definition and development. Additionally, I actively promoted the use of best practices, software development tools, and the team's technical improvement.
My main responsibilities encompassed:
Back-end development of microservices applications using NET;
Front-end development utilizing AngularJS and ReactJS;
Utilization of relational databases such as SQL Server, MySQL, distributed cache systems like Redis, event streaming with Kafka, search indexers such as Elasticsearch, and non-relational databases like Cassandra;
Monitoring activities using Grafana Prometheus, SEQ, NagiosXI, and Jaeger;
Adoption of CI/CD tools such as Azure DevOps, TeamCity, and Octopus;
Effective utilization of code versioning tools, particularly Git;
Conducting code analysis to drive the implementation of new features, improve architecture, and troubleshoot issues.
Throughout my experience, I developed competencies in Redis, Elasticsearch, React.js, Apache Kafka, JavaScript, Microsoft Azure, C#, Grafana, and Kubernetes. This comprehensive skill set enabled me to contribute effectively to the team's objectives and deliver high-quality solutions to clients and partners.

- Sales tracking;
- Customer service and acquisition;
- Delivery Implementation (System, techniques, process);
- Implementation of the sales control system.

As a Software Engineer at Motorola Solutions, I craft robust software for the Public Safety sector. In my role in the interfaces team, I develop and integrate APIs to enhance Motorola's software connectivity with external systems. My role demands fluent English communication and direct coordination with our US-based team.

Daily Responsibilities:
- Develop scalable, reliable code in Java, C#, C, and Angular, ensuring high efficiency and performance;
- Design and implement APIs, facilitating seamless integration with external systems, crucial for enhancing public safety operations;
- Conduct comprehensive testing, including end-to-end and unit tests, to ensure the trustworthiness and reliability of the software;
- Collaborate with global teams, requiring effective communication in English to coordinate with colleagues based in the US.

Technologies Used:
- Java, C#, C for backend development;
- AngularJS for frontend development;
- REST API, and SOAP;
- XML, JSON for data interchange;
- Use of development and testing methodologies to maintain code quality and application performance.

- Production planning assistance;
- Production tracking;
- Production orders conference;
- Participation in system implementation.

